Thank you very much, sir!

24:23.525 --> 24:26.767
You bastard! You and me are
gonna go at it someday, Jack!

24:26.861 --> 24:27.901
We're gonna remember this!

24:27.988 --> 24:29.023
I hope you rot and die!

24:29.197 --> 24:30.903
You sick bastard!

24:31.032 --> 24:32.032
Shit...

24:37.580 --> 24:39.195
Yamagata!

24:39.332 --> 24:41.118
What happened to your cheek?

24:41.251 --> 24:42.457
Shut the hell up.

24:42.585 --> 24:44.450
Let me guess, jaws from p.E.?

24:44.546 --> 24:47.288
They say you fought the
clowns on a highway in the old city!

24:47.382 --> 24:48.087
Yeah.

24:48.216 --> 24:51.208
Why don't you just wipe 'em out?
Those guys are so gross!

24:51.344 --> 24:52.709
And last night...

24:52.887 --> 24:54.865
There were demonstrators,
cops, and even the damn army!

24:54.889 --> 24:56.800
And that idiot tetsuo had an accident, too.

24:56.891 --> 24:58.552
What happened to tetsuo?

24:58.643 --> 25:00.705
He's in the hospital.
I guess, but we don't know where.

25:00.729 --> 25:02.765
The idiot was trying to show off.

25:05.942 --> 25:07.102
That idiot...

25:07.235 --> 25:09.066
What, you mean tetsuo?

25:09.154 --> 25:12.146
Shut up! I've had enough
of your damn flirting!

25:12.240 --> 25:14.401
What's gotten into you?!

25:29.507 --> 25:32.920
Tetsuo? It's time for your medication.

25:34.054 --> 25:36.921
Doctor! There's a problem!

25:40.727 --> 25:45.391
I can't. The dorm mother
throws a fit if you go out before 10.

25:45.565 --> 25:48.432
Yeah, the one with the face like a goat.

25:48.526 --> 25:52.439
That old bag's such a pain...
She's always yammering on and on and on.

25:52.572 --> 25:55.188
Tomorrow at three? Sure, that'd be okay.

25:55.325 --> 25:58.533
Hey, what happened
to that girl a while back?

25:58.620 --> 26:02.784
I don't like her much.
Her personality just gets on my nerves.

26:02.957 --> 26:04.037
Kaori...

26:06.252 --> 26:07.742
Tetsuo!

26:08.171 --> 26:12.505
Everyone's been worried about you!
They thought you might be dead.

26:18.973 --> 26:23.387
When I woke up, I was on an
operating table or something.

26:23.520 --> 26:25.636
And that examination...

26:25.730 --> 26:30.144
It's like... they were messing
around inside my head.

26:30.318 --> 26:32.809
I don't want to go back there.

26:32.987 --> 26:34.648
Let's run away...

26:34.739 --> 26:36.149
Where?

26:37.575 --> 26:42.160
Someplace. Someplace far away.

26:44.958 --> 26:46.823
- What's your problem?
- That's mine!

26:46.960 --> 26:47.960
I wanna get laid!

26:48.044 --> 26:49.750
Hey! Today's independent study!

26:49.838 --> 26:55.083
Say what? What about
my burning desire to study?!

26:55.218 --> 26:56.754
Drag his butt in here!

26:58.096 --> 26:59.927
Kaneda! Your bike!

27:00.056 --> 27:01.341
My bike?

27:02.892 --> 27:03.927
Look!

27:07.522 --> 27:08.762
Tetsuo!

27:11.192 --> 27:12.398
Are you sure this is okay?

27:12.527 --> 27:14.939
Shut up! Just keep quiet and hang on!

27:18.533 --> 27:24.278
"Off limits"

27:26.040 --> 27:26.870
huh?

27:27.041 --> 27:28.372
Whats wrong?

27:30.420 --> 27:31.535
Shit!

27:31.671 --> 27:31.909
Oh, no...

27:31.921 --> 27:32.535
'End the shimamoto labor union's
lllegal strike!!” oh, no...

27:32.547 --> 27:32.706
"End the shimamoto
labor union's illegal strike!!”

27:32.714 --> 27:36.047
"End the shimamoto labor union's lllegal
strike!!” we're stopping... we stopped.

27:36.050 --> 27:36.459
"End the shimamoto
labor union's illegal strike!!”

27:36.467 --> 27:37.297
'End the shimamoto labor union's illegal strike!!" Oh, okay. The
engine can't drop below 5,000 even when you're changing gears.

27:37.302 --> 27:40.886
Oh, okay. The engine can't drop below
5,000 even when you're changing gears.

27:41.055 --> 27:43.387
- My butt hurts.
- Okay, I get it...

27:43.558 --> 27:44.798
Look, hikes!

27:46.144 --> 27:47.884
Is that kaneda and...?

27:48.062 --> 27:50.144
It's not them!

27:53.401 --> 27:54.641
Kaori!

27:58.323 --> 27:59.563
Any sign of him?

27:59.699 --> 28:01.906
Kuwata and the others
went to look around kisarazu.

28:02.035 --> 28:04.742
All that's left now is the industrial area!

28:04.871 --> 28:06.827
Okay, let's go!

28:09.751 --> 28:12.914
We owe you for the other night!

28:21.471 --> 28:22.756
Shut up!

28:25.683 --> 28:27.969
Kaori! What did they do, kaori?!

28:34.692 --> 28:39.937
Don't! If you so much as scratch
that bike, I'm gonna kill you!

28:45.787 --> 28:46.947
Run!

28:47.080 --> 28:48.445
Don't let 'em get away!

28:55.421 --> 28:56.421
Wait!

29:06.140 --> 29:07.721
Tetsuo!

29:14.190 --> 29:17.557
"Smash the strike!”

29:24.742 --> 29:27.154
That's enough, tetsuo!
Are you trying to kill him?

29:27.287 --> 29:30.154
Yes! I'm gonna kill him!
I'll split his damn head open!

29:30.290 --> 29:32.030
Knock it off!

29:32.166 --> 29:36.000
This happened because
you took my bike for a joyride.

29:36.087 --> 29:36.951
Enough, already!

29:37.046 --> 29:40.664
Shut up! Don't order me around!

29:40.842 --> 29:42.503
We were worried about you.

29:42.593 --> 29:45.756
Why do you always have
to come and save me?

29:46.472 --> 29:50.932
I could've handled it myself!
I admit I got beat up that one time,

29:51.019 --> 29:54.386
but I won't always be on the receiving end!

29:54.856 --> 29:56.972
Understand?!

30:00.987 --> 30:02.443
Tetsuo...

30:03.698 --> 30:05.689
Shut up! Stay away from me!

30:07.994 --> 30:10.076
Hey, wait! Where are you going?

30:11.706 --> 30:12.912
Leave me alone!

30:15.376 --> 30:16.376
Akira'

30:20.715 --> 30:21.795
tetsuo!

30:25.053 --> 30:26.293
Whats wrong?

30:27.221 --> 30:28.131
Akira'

30:28.222 --> 30:30.053
I don't know who that is!

30:52.622 --> 30:54.908
Tetsuo, are you...

30:54.999 --> 30:56.239
Hey!

31:00.713 --> 31:02.419
This is strange.

31:02.548 --> 31:05.415
I'm getting a blue pattern on scope ♪3!

31:05.551 --> 31:08.588
Oh, no! Retrieve the subject! Hurry!

31:22.443 --> 31:24.980
What're you doing to my friend?!

31:28.533 --> 31:32.617
What's with you?
You just come back from a funeral?

31:39.127 --> 31:40.537
Tetsuo!

31:40.795 --> 31:41.875
Kaneda!

31:43.464 --> 31:44.829
Shit...

31:54.350 --> 31:55.465
Wait!

32:02.358 --> 32:04.565
Hey, kaneda...

32:15.955 --> 32:20.995
I see we have some youngsters doing their
thing in spite of the tight checkpoints.

32:21.335 --> 32:24.418
That just means that
they're stupid, don't it?

32:28.176 --> 32:32.510
This is boring. Hey, let's go home.

32:32.638 --> 32:34.253
But it's still early!

32:34.348 --> 32:38.261
Yeah, but without their bikes
they're just skirt-chasers out of water.

32:38.352 --> 32:39.717
You mean "fish"!

32:39.854 --> 32:42.766
Come on, let's go. Let's
toss these fish back!

32:43.149 --> 32:46.266
Hey, kaneda, what're we gonna do?

32:49.238 --> 32:50.523
What the...?

32:50.656 --> 32:51.691
Look!

33:18.017 --> 33:19.097
Thats...

33:19.560 --> 33:23.394
Here we go again... let's get out
of here before we get involved again.

33:23.523 --> 33:25.388
Huh?

33:25.483 --> 33:26.483
Kaneda?

33:26.609 --> 33:27.689
Hey!

33:29.237 --> 33:33.401
This area is being cordoned
off due to a terrorist bombing.

33:33.533 --> 33:35.653
Those who wish fo get
through, line up in single file,

33:35.701 --> 33:39.068
present your ID and go
through the checkpoint.

33:49.382 --> 33:50.747
Get in.

33:50.883 --> 33:54.125
What's wrong? Hurry. I'll
be right behind you.

33:55.054 --> 33:56.919
You know the rendezvous point, right?

33:58.057 --> 34:01.265
- Be careful.
- You too, ryu.

34:08.109 --> 34:10.270
Were the clowns”

34:14.448 --> 34:16.860
stop! Stop, damn it!

34:18.828 --> 34:20.284
She's got a gun!

34:31.841 --> 34:33.957
Okay, that's far enough!

34:34.135 --> 34:35.295
Drop the gun!

34:42.810 --> 34:44.391
Drop it now!

34:50.359 --> 34:51.974
Stop!

35:05.458 --> 35:07.323
I think it came from over here!

35:07.418 --> 35:09.158
- There were two shots!
- No, three!

35:09.253 --> 35:10.914
It's just up ahead!

35:11.005 --> 35:13.747
Hey. Let's get out of here.

35:13.841 --> 35:14.956
Come on!

35:42.995 --> 35:48.706
Tdiot I moron I fool I no. 1"

36:21.492 --> 36:22.732
Kaneda!

36:48.561 --> 36:52.600
So, what's the matter?
Try telling me about it.

36:52.732 --> 36:55.439
1 had a dream.

36:55.568 --> 36:57.104
A dream?

36:58.654 --> 37:03.569
The city will be covered by a
dark shadow and start to crumble.

37:03.868 --> 37:06.280
Lots of people died...

37:06.454 --> 37:10.697
And we met Akira again.

37:10.833 --> 37:12.118
Akira?!

37:12.209 --> 37:19.297
The city will crumble,
and so many people will die...

37:19.383 --> 37:23.126
When?! When will it happen, kiyoko?!

37:23.304 --> 37:26.216
You mustn't let that boy go.

37:26.348 --> 37:29.465
His power, it...

37:35.941 --> 37:36.941
What did she mean?!

37:37.026 --> 37:42.896
Well, there's nothing
physically wrong with her.

37:42.990 --> 37:44.400
Her medication is normal. Too.

37:44.492 --> 37:48.952
There's no sign of any abnormalities
in her ecg or eeg, either.

37:49.163 --> 37:54.829
I think what number 25 said
was her precognitive power at work.

37:54.919 --> 37:59.583
This must be presented to the supreme
executive council for inquiry, but...

37:59.715 --> 38:01.501
Do you believe her?

38:01.634 --> 38:03.920
I have no doubts
regarding number 25's abilities.

38:04.053 --> 38:06.840
We have all sorts of data
that substantiate her abilities.

38:07.014 --> 38:08.720
What about you, colonel?

38:09.683 --> 38:14.222
My job isn't to believe or disbelieve.
It's to act or not to act.

38:26.826 --> 38:27.861
Here, sir.

38:27.952 --> 38:31.740
Cold gear, colonel.
Please put it on. You, too, doctor.

38:43.551 --> 38:48.215
The other day, a young
researcher asked me something.

38:48.347 --> 38:52.386
He wondered if their power was the form the
next stage of human evolution was faking,

38:52.518 --> 38:57.012
and perhaps that well all
be able to control it someday.

38:58.107 --> 39:00.894
Scientists are a bunch of romantics.

39:00.985 --> 39:04.068
Military men always
consider the risks first.

39:04.154 --> 39:06.736
It's taken thirty long years.

39:06.866 --> 39:10.734
We've come so far from the rubble.

39:10.870 --> 39:13.077
We can't just trade one for the other.

39:13.205 --> 39:17.744
I've always thought that
you hated this city, colonel.

39:17.835 --> 39:23.171
The passion to build has cooled
and the joy of reconstruction forgotten,

39:23.299 --> 39:27.292
and now it's just a garbage heap
made up of hedonistic fools.

39:27.428 --> 39:30.795
So you're trying to save the city, then.

39:31.181 --> 39:34.844
It's how a soldier thinks.
A scientist wouldn't understand.

39:38.439 --> 39:40.600
Colonel, we're here.

39:40.691 --> 39:41.691
This way, sir.

40:02.212 --> 40:05.625
Room 10, 148 degrees Kelvin.

40:05.966 --> 40:08.628
Fluctuation tolerance range, check.

40:08.719 --> 40:13.213
Room 9, 118 degrees Kelvin.
Fluctuation tolerance, check.

40:13.307 --> 40:16.049
Emergency power generator, check.

40:16.185 --> 40:17.185
Open it.

40:17.227 --> 40:18.467
Yes, sir.

40:18.604 --> 40:19.218
Uh...

40:19.313 --> 40:20.428
Go to the control room!

40:20.522 --> 40:21.557
Yes, sir!

40:38.457 --> 40:44.327
Room 1 is at 0.0005 degrees Kelvin.
It's within tolerances.

40:44.505 --> 40:49.215
No abnormalities detected in any of the
rooms' dewar walls or in the defense system.

40:49.593 --> 40:53.177
No abnormal atmospheric
concentrations or reactions recorded.

40:53.430 --> 40:55.671
All systems nominal, then?

41:05.150 --> 41:08.438
Look at what they abandoned
in their panic. They were afraid!

41:08.529 --> 41:10.895
They were too scared,
so they hid it away from the public.

41:11.115 --> 41:13.527
They forgot all shame and honor

41:13.617 --> 41:17.951
and cast off the civilization
and science we had created,

41:18.080 --> 41:22.619
and shut the lid of the pandora's box
they themselves had opened.

41:27.131 --> 41:27.790
Ryu!

41:27.881 --> 41:30.122
Hey, we're still young.

41:30.217 --> 41:32.799
1 think we can start over.

41:32.886 --> 41:34.126
I'll go with you to the police.

41:34.304 --> 41:35.304
Ryu!

41:35.347 --> 41:36.803
Come on, turn yourself in!

41:36.890 --> 41:39.077
That was the first time you
ever killed somebody, right?

41:39.101 --> 41:39.715
Ryu!

41:39.852 --> 41:42.764
Anyway, once you've
purified your body and soul,

41:42.896 --> 41:45.228
let's go out for tea or something.

41:45.315 --> 41:47.226
Don't kick yourself over it, okay?

41:47.359 --> 41:51.227
What's done is done. The guy's dead.

41:58.245 --> 41:59.781
Who're you?!

42:00.664 --> 42:03.246
Ryu! You're okay!

42:03.375 --> 42:05.582
- Kei, is that you?
- Ryu!

42:06.295 --> 42:08.206
Who's this?

42:08.464 --> 42:09.874
Who, me?

42:10.007 --> 42:15.923
Well, I guess saying I'm kei's
boyfriend might be stretching it a bit.

42:16.096 --> 42:19.588
But we havent gotten physical
or anything yet, understand?

42:19.683 --> 42:20.718
Are you a spy?! No!

42:20.809 --> 42:22.265
Liar!

42:26.857 --> 42:28.438
Is he really okay?

42:28.609 --> 42:31.726
All 1 know for sure is that he's not a spy.

42:32.029 --> 42:33.690
Ow...

42:35.282 --> 42:37.238
Sneak into their lab?!

42:37.534 --> 42:40.071
Are you serious? Don't you
remember the fiasco with that kid?!

42:40.245 --> 42:43.863
Last-minute orders.
Besides, the plan's already in place.

42:46.835 --> 42:49.622
The lab passes that they
issue once a week...

42:49.755 --> 42:51.416
They're from Mr. nezu?

42:51.799 --> 42:53.130
What's the objective?

42:53.258 --> 42:55.795
Detailed data on the new subject.

42:55.969 --> 42:57.459
New subject?

42:57.596 --> 43:04.638
Yes. Last week, on the night we tried
to abduct the subject called number 26,

43:04.812 --> 43:09.476
a hoy who was in an accident on an
old city highway was brought to the lab.

43:09.650 --> 43:12.141
Looks like he's a student
at a vocational training school.

43:12.277 --> 43:15.644
But he's now their new subject
for human experimentation.

43:19.660 --> 43:20.820
Ow!

43:20.911 --> 43:24.244
Ow! What's the big idea?!

43:24.581 --> 43:25.411
You!

43:25.499 --> 43:26.989
He heard us! Let's kill him!

43:27.126 --> 43:27.740
Ryu!

43:27.835 --> 43:31.748
W-wait a minute! Listen to me!
Listen to what I have to say!

43:31.839 --> 43:32.874
He saved me!

43:33.006 --> 43:34.166
Twice!

43:34.258 --> 43:36.249
Maybe it was just to get close to us.

43:36.343 --> 43:39.801
The guy who was in that accident
in the old city is a friend of mine!

43:40.013 --> 43:43.050
I know it's hard to believe,
but it's the truth!

43:43.183 --> 43:45.845
I was there when it happened!

43:45.978 --> 43:49.766
Don't they say the only foolish
questions are unasked ones?

43:49.898 --> 43:52.480
Huh? They don't?

43:53.902 --> 43:56.939
That's an intriguing story.

43:57.197 --> 44:00.030
Will you be taking the boy with you?

44:00.117 --> 44:04.486
He knows the subject, and I think
we can use him as a decoy if necessary.

44:04.830 --> 44:08.072
Neo Tokyo is going to change.

44:08.834 --> 44:14.045
In all respects, this city is
saturated. It's like an overripe fruit.

44:14.173 --> 44:16.789
And within it is a new seed.

44:16.884 --> 44:20.968
We only need to wait for
the wind which will make it fall.

44:21.054 --> 44:23.887
The wind called Akira!

44:24.266 --> 44:27.224
Ryu, look!

44:27.936 --> 44:28.936
What is it?

44:28.979 --> 44:31.561
We aren't the ones who will change it,

44:31.773 --> 44:35.812
but rather, those citizens
who hope for Akira will.

44:35.903 --> 44:39.737
That which is called
science perverts Providence!

44:39.823 --> 44:42.360
That which is called progress
encourages extravagance!

44:42.367 --> 44:43.026
